    "_meanings": [
        ".²1 <ab>N.</ab> of the son of Duṣyanta and Śakuntalā, who became a universal\n monarch ({#cakravartin#}), India being called {%Bharatavarṣa%} after\n him. He was one of the remote ancestors of the Kauravas and Pāṇḍavas; <ab>cf.</ab> <ls>Ś. 7. 33</ls>.\n",
        ".²2 <ab>N.</ab> of a brother of Rāma, son of Kaikeyī, the youngest wife of Daśaratha.\n He was very pious and righteous, and was so much devoted to Rāma that\n when the latter prepared to go to the forest in accordance with the wicked\n demand of Kaikeyī, he was very much grieved to find that his own mother\n had sent his brother into exile, and refusing the sovereignty that was\n his own, ruled the kingdom in the name of Rāma (by bringing from him\n his two sandals and making them the ‘regents’ of the realm) till he returned\n after his fourteen yearsʼ exile. {#Barato nAma kEkeyyAM jajYe satyaparAkramaH .#}\n {#sAkzAdvizRoScaturBAgaH sarvEH samudito guREH ..#} <ls>Rām. 1. 18. 13</ls>.\n",
        ".²3 <ab>N.</ab> of an ancient sage who is supposed to have been the founder of the\n science of music and dramaturgy.\n",
        ".²4 An actor, a stage-player; {#tatkimityudAsate BaratAH#} <ls>Māl. 1</ls>.\n",
        ".²5 A hired soldier, mercenary.\n",
        ".²6 A barbarian, mountaineer.\n",
        ".²7 An epithet of Agni.\n",
        ".²8 A weaver.\n",
        ".²9 <ab>N.</ab> of the sage Jaḍabharata.\n"
    ],
